{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A maskil of Asaph</b> — a piyyut whose beginning is <i>maskil</i> or <i>maskil ha-shome'a</i> [the maskil who hears]. The meaning of the construct attached to it is <i>the Torah of YHWH</i>, which is the Torah of his faith. And the correct interpretation is like: <i>the words of my mouth</i> [in construct] to one who wishes to instruct, in the manner of <i>the Torah of your mother</i>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:52.633390681Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}